diff --git a/01-client/audit/review-package/commit-message.txt b/01-client/audit/review-package/commit-message.txt
index 1a37b4b..734cf07 100644
--- a/01-client/audit/review-package/commit-message.txt
+++ b/01-client/audit/review-package/commit-message.txt
@@ -1,32 +1,28 @@
-fix(settings): write-only secrets, fail-closed encryption and bounded settings
+fix(settings): encrypt Forms CAPTCHA secrets, clear both Stripe modes, drop test seams
 
-Stripe secret key and webhook secret are now write-only. Inputs render
-empty, a blank field keeps the stored value, and new secrets are
-encrypted or the save is refused (it used to fall back to plaintext).
-Legacy plaintext keys are still upgraded to enc:v1 envelopes on save.
-The Forms CAPTCHA secret is write-only, with an explicit clear checkbox.
-Backups, Booking and MCP no longer 500 when encryption throws: the
-affected secret is skipped and an error is shown.
+Forms CAPTCHA secrets are now stored as enc:v1 envelopes. The editor
+refuses to save a new secret when encryption is unavailable, a blank
+field keeps the stored value, a legacy plaintext secret is upgraded on
+save, and the clear checkbox removes it. The public form decrypts the
+secret before calling the provider and rejects submissions if it cannot.
 
-Settings: permalink structure is allow-listed to the form's choices,
-start_of_week is limited to 0..6, backup retention to 1..365, and only
-the Date & Time tab writes timezone. Brand font and radius are emitted
-as CSS variables. Coaching settings saves are audit-logged.
+Stripe "Disconnect" now clears the test and live key slots as well as
+the legacy ones, so Stripe really is disconnected, and records
+stripe.keys_cleared. Countries and toggles are left alone.
 
-Identity tokens are stamped on the database clock, matching
-consumeToken(). Before this, a PHP/MySQL timezone gap expired tokens
-immediately.
+Remove the PaymentButtonRenderer::$stripeReadyOverride test seam. The
+old order-dependent failure was a missing APP_SECRET once the real
+slate_sign() was loaded; the test now defines it and verifies through
+slate_sign(). Remove the react-site-bridge tests, which could never
+run because that plugin was never committed. Run the platform-admin
+negative upload test with the plugin lock open, and mirror the client
+clock fixture into the licensing ContactSeeder and CustomerAuthParity
+tests.
 
-Adds archive/.htaccess (Require all denied) in both trees, French
-strings for the new UI text, SystemSettingsAuditFixesTest (static checks
-of the shipped files) and StripeWriteOnlySecretTest (end-to-end save
-and render). Fixes the POST probe's unlock flag clashing with its
-tenant-override argument. Brings the stale integration tests in line
-with Phase 13 remote authority and the plugin lock.
-
-Client integration goes from 608/631 to 634/634; unit suites are green
-in both trees. Licensing integration is 351/403 per file, with the same
-52 failures as before this change. The audit documents and evidence
-are in 01-client/audit/review-package/.
+Correct the inventory against source: 52 rows renamed to real keys, 38
+rows for settings that do not exist moved to a removed-rows file with
+reasons, 1 marked not implemented, 1 added. Regenerate the widget
+matrix from the renderer registry, and refresh the review package and
+test evidence against origin/main.
 
